    "interpretation": "H2FillS documents a station-to-FCEV model validated against empirical fueling data; H2-Stations and the European Hydrogen Observatory expose station registry/availability/storage/inventory data; the DLR/FCH2RAIL paper shows example measurement traces. The CARB official infrastructure portal and 2024 report state that Appendix A results were tabulated in an Excel workbook for 22 in-use HRS tests, but the public route exposes only the report PDF and no appendix workbook/logger link, so the workbook/logger remains a custodian-request candidate. The OEDI H2SAFE ZIP is an admissible public helium detector/dispersion component dataset with spatial metadata, but has no vehicle-side or station-to-vehicle fueling channels. Cal State LA publications provide stronger provenance for a real station raw-dataset request because they state that per-fill or one-year back-to-back data were collected, but their public routes expose no machine-readable synchronized export or reuse terms. None was admitted as a reusable synchronized station-to-vehicle raw logger bundle in this release."
